---
import translator from "../../i18n/translator";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const { translate } = translator(Astro);
---

<Base baseRoute="/">
  <h1>A Discord bot for harm reduction and chemistry.</h1>
  <img
    class="hero"
    src="/img/psychotropic.svg"
    alt={translate("site.altLogo")}
  />
  <p>
    Psychotropic provides various information about chemicals, psychoactives,
    their properties and uses.
  </p>
  <a
    class="cta"
    href="https://discord.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=665177975053877259&scope=bot+applications.commands&permissions=277025442880"
    >Add me to your guild!</a
  >

  <h2 id="license">License</h2>
  <p>
    Psychotropic is open source software, distributed under the <a
      href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html"
      rel="external nofollow">GNU GPL v3</a
    > license. Source code is avalaible <a
      href="https://github.com/x-yzt/psychotropic"
      rel="external nofollow">here</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2 id="terms-of-use">Terms of Use</h2>

  <h3>1. Acceptance of Terms</h3>
  <p>
    By adding Psychotropic to a server, interacting with it, or using any of its
    commands or features, you agree to these Terms of Service ("Terms") and to
    our <a href="#privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you add Psychotropic to a server, you confirm that you have the authority
    to do so and that you accept these Terms on behalf of that server.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Purpose and Nature of the Service</h3>
  <p>
    Psychotropic provides <b>educational information</b> about chemistry, pharmacology,
    psychoactive substances, their effects, risks, and traditional or therapeutic
    uses, with a focus on <b>harm reduction</b>: reducing the health and social
    risks associated with substance use, regardless of its legal status.
  </p>
  <p><b>Psychotropic is not:</b></p>
  <ul>
    <li>a medical, psychiatric, pharmaceutical, or legal service;</li>
    <li>
      a substitute for a doctor, pharmacist, addiction specialist, or emergency
      services;
    </li>
    <li>
      a source of diagnosis, treatment, prescriptions, or personalized dosing
      advice;
    </li>
    <li>a marketplace, vendor directory, or sourcing tool.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing Psychotropic provides is a recommendation or encouragement to use
    any substance.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Eligibility</h3>
  <p>
    You must be at least <b>18 years old</b> (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction,
    if higher) to use Psychotropic. You must also meet the minimum age required by
    Discord's Terms of Service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Server administrators must ensure Psychotropic is used only in appropriately
    age-restricted channels where required by Discord's policies and applicable
    law.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Medical and Safety Disclaimer</h3>
  <p>
    <b>Information may be incomplete, outdated, or inaccurate.</b> Responses may include
    automated content and may contain errors. Effects, risks, and interactions vary
    greatly between individuals based on health, genetics, medication, dose, setting,
    and purity.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>No substance is risk-free.</b> Information about safer use does not mean
      a substance or behavior is safe.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Always consult a qualified healthcare professional</b> before making decisions
      about your health, medications, or substance use.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>In an emergency, contact local emergency services immediately</b> or a poison
      control center. Do not rely on Psychotropic or wait for a reply in a medical
      emergency.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Psychotropic may display crisis and support resources. These are provided
    for convenience and are not guaranteed to be available, complete, or
    current.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Prohibited Uses</h3>
  <p>You agree <b>not</b> to use Psychotropic to:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <b
        >Request or obtain synthesis, extraction, production, or manufacturing
        instructions</b
      > for controlled or illegal substances, explosives, or weapons or their precursors;
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Buy, sell, trade, source, or advertise</b> controlled substances, or locate
      vendors, markets, or dealers;
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Encourage or pressure others</b> to use substances, or promote drug use to
      minors or vulnerable people;
    </li>
    <li><b>Evade law enforcement</b> or commit any unlawful act;</li>
    <li>
      <b>Scrape or bulk-extract</b> Psychotropic's content for commercial redistribution
      or to train other models without permission;
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Violate</b> the Discord Terms of Service, Community Guidelines, or Developer
      Policy.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h3>6. Legal Compliance and User Responsibility</h3>
  <p>
    Laws on psychoactive substances differ widely and change often.
    <b>You alone are responsible</b> for knowing and complying with the laws of your
    jurisdiction. Information about a substance's effects, uses, or safer-use practices
    does not mean it is legal where you live. We make no representation that Psychotropic's
    content is lawful or appropriate in every location.
  </p>
  <p>
    You use all information <b>at your own risk</b> and are solely responsible for
    your choices and their consequences.
  </p>

  <h3>7. Server Administrator Responsibilities</h3>
  <p>If you administer a server that uses Psychotropic, you agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      configure channels and permissions appropriately, including age-gating
      where required;
    </li>
    <li>
      moderate use of Psychotropic in your server and enforce these Terms;
    </li>
    <li>
      not present Psychotropic as a medical service or as endorsed by us beyond
      what is stated here.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>8. Data and Privacy</h3>
  <p>
    We collect and process limited data to operate Psychotropic (such as Discord
    user and server IDs, commands and inputs, and technical logs). Because
    substance-use information can be sensitive, we:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>collect only what is necessary;</li>
    <li>do not sell personal data;</li>
    <li>do not perform any generative model training on personal data;</li>
    <li>do not store the content of conversations.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Details, including your rights to access, correct, delete, or port your data
    (including under the <b>GDPR</b> if you are in the EEA/UK), are in our
    <a href="#privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We recommand that you <b>do not share sensitive personal information</b> (such
    as your full name, address, or health records) with Psychotropic or in public
    channels.
  </p>

  <h3>9. Intellectual Property and License</h3>
  <p>
    <b>Source code.</b> Psychotropic's source code is free software released under
    the GNU General Public License version 3 ("GPL-3.0"). Your rights to use, study,
    modify, and redistribute the code are set out in that license. Nothing in these
    Terms restricts the rights the GPL-3.0 grants you.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Hosted service.</b> These Terms govern your use of the instance of Psychotropic
    that we operate (the "Service"), not the source code. If you run your own copy
    of Psychotropic, you are the operator of that copy, these Terms do not apply to
    it, and you are solely responsible for its content, data handling, and legal compliance.
    You may not present your copy as the official Service or imply that we endorse
    or are responsible for it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Content and data.</b> Unless stated otherwise, documentation and informational
    content published with Psychotropic is in the public domain. Some content may
    be adapted from third-party sources and remains subject to the rights and licenses
    of its owners.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Name and branding.</b> Psychotropic's name, logo, and visual identity are not
    licensed under the GPL-3.0. You may not use them in a way that suggests affiliation
    with or endorsement by us, except as permitted by law or by a separate written
    permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Contributions.</b> Unless we agree otherwise in writing, anything you contribute
    to Psychotropic's source code is licensed under the same terms as the code, the
    GPL-3.0.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>Warranty.</b> For the source code, the warranty disclaimer and limitation of
    liability in the GPL-3.0 apply. Sections 13 and 14 of these Terms apply to the
    Service.
  </p>

  <h3>10. Third-Party Services and Links</h3>
  <p>
    Psychotropic runs on Discord and may link to or rely on third-party
    resources (e.g., harm reduction organizations, databases, or drug-checking
    services). We do not control and are not responsible for third-party
    content, services, or availability.
  </p>

  <h3>11. Availability and Changes to the Service</h3>
  <p>
    Psychotropic is provided on a best-effort basis. We may modify, suspend,
    limit, or discontinue any part of it at any time, with or without notice,
    including to comply with law or platform requirements.
  </p>

  <h3>12. Suspension and Termination</h3>
  <p>
    You may stop using Psychotropic at any time by removing it from your server.
  </p>

  <h3>13. Disclaimer of Warranties</h3>
  <p>
    TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, PSYCHOTROPIC AND ALL CONTENT ARE
    PROVIDED <b>"AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE"</b> WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
    OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, RELIABILITY, MERCHANTABILITY,
    FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT
    PSYCHOTROPIC WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR SECURE.
  </p>

  <h3>14. Limitation of Liability</h3>
  <p>
    TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, WE AND OUR CONTRIBUTORS, VOLUNTEERS,
    AND AFFILIATES WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
    CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF HEALTH, LIFE, DATA,
    PROFITS, OR REPUTATION, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR RELIANCE ON PSYCHOTROPIC
    OR ITS CONTENT, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, including limitations
    of liability for death, personal injury, gross negligence, or intentional
    misconduct. In those cases, our liability is limited to the maximum extent
    permitted by law. Nothing in these Terms limits any rights you have as a
    consumer under mandatory law.
  </p>

  <h3>15. Changes to These Terms</h3>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use after the
    effective date means you accept the revised Terms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="privacy-policy">Privacy policy</h2>

  <h3>1. Object of This Policy</h3>
  <p>
    We are the <b>data controller</b> for the personal data described here under the
    EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the UK GDPR where applicable.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact <a href="https://github.com/x-yzt" rel="external nofollow">xyzt_</a> for
    all privacy matters.
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy applies to the instance of Psychotropic that we operate. If
    someone runs their own copy of Psychotropic's open-source code, they are the
    controller for that copy.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Data We Process</h3>
  <p>
    Psychotropic mainly works through Discord's interactions (slash commands,
    buttons, and similar components). It also uses Discord's <b
      >Message Content intent</b
    > so that it can read messages in channels where a game is running and detect
    players' guesses.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Uses</th><th>Stored?</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><b>Message content</b></td>
        <td>Detect whether a message contains a correct guess</td>
        <td>
          No. Processed in memory only, then discarded. We do not save, log,
          copy, or share it.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><b>User ID</b></td>
        <td>Attribute scores to the right player</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><b>Display name</b></td>
        <td>Show you on leaderboards</td>
        <td>No (fetched live)</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><b>Game scores and statistics</b></td>
        <td>Run leaderboards</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><b>Server (guild) and channel IDs</b></td>
        <td>Technical purposes</td>
        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><b>Technical logs</b></td>
        <td>Technical purposes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <b>Note on message content:</b> because Psychotropic can read messages in channels
    where a game is active, it technically sees messages from everyone writing there,
    including people who are not playing. It only checks them against the current
    game and keeps nothing. Discord, as an independent controller, holds your messages.
  </p>
  <p>No data is used for generative models training.</p>

  <h3>3. Who We Share Data With</h3>
  <p>
    Your display name and your scores appear on leaderboards that are visible to
    other users of Psychotropic, which may include people outside your server.
    If you do not want to appear, you can contact us, and we will remove or
    anonymize your entry. Upon deletion of your Discord account, your scores
    will be anonymized.
  </p>

  <p>
    We do <b>not</b> sell your personal data or share it for advertising. Data is
    shared only with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>Discord Inc.</b>, which runs the platform and is an independent
      controller of the data it holds about you. See <a
        href="https://discord.com/privacy"
        rel="external nofollow">Discord's Privacy Policy</a
      >;
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Our hosting provider</b>, acting as a processor that stores
      Psychotropic's database.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>4. International Transfers</h3>
  <p>
    Discord operates globally, including in the United States, and handles
    transfers under its own safeguards. If we or our processors transfer
    personal data outside the EEA/UK, we rely on an adequacy decision, the EU-US
    Data Privacy Framework where the recipient is certified, or Standard
    Contractual Clauses, as applicable.
  </p>

  <h3>5. Your Rights</h3>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <b>Access</b> the personal data we hold about you and receive a copy;
    </li>
    <li><b>Rectify</b> inaccurate data;</li>
    <li><b>Erase</b> your data ("right to be forgotten");</li>
    <li><b>Restrict</b> processing in certain cases;</li>
    <li>
      <b>Data portability</b>, to receive your data in a structured,
      machine-readable format;
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>Object</b> to processing based on legitimate interests, including appearing
      on leaderboards.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use these rights, contact us. We may need to verify that you control the
    Discord account concerned. We respond within <b>one month</b>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You also have the right to <b>lodge a complaint</b> with a data protection authority,
    in particular in the EU/EEA country where you live, work, or where you believe
    an infringement occurred (for example, the CNIL in France, or the ICO in the UK).
    A list is available at <a
      href="https://edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/about-edpb/members_en"
    >
      edpb.europa.eu
    </a>. We would appreciate the chance to resolve your concern first.
  </p>

  <h3>6. Children</h3>
  <p>
    You must meet Discord's minimum age requirement and be at least 18 under our
    Terms of Service. If we learn that we hold data about someone who does not
    meet these requirements, we will delete it. If you believe this has
    happened, contact us.
  </p>

  <h3>7. Security</h3>
  <p>
    We use appropriate technical and organizational measures to protect data,
    such as access controls, restricted credentials, encrypted connections, and
    limited data collection. No system is completely secure. If a breach is
    likely to put your rights at risk, we will notify the relevant authority
    within 72 hours and inform you where required by law.
  </p>

  <h3>8. Changes to This Policy</h3>
  <p>
    We may update this Policy from time to time. Continued use after the
    effective date means you accept the revised Policy.
  </p>

  <slot name="after-content" />
</Base>
